<article class="env-lemma" id="02NM">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02NM">Lemma <span data-tag="02NM">29.30.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite presentation, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $s \in S$ the fibre $X_ s$ is Cohen-Macaulay (Properties, Definition <a href="/tag/02IO" data-tag="02IO">28.8.1</a>) 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exist open and closed subschemes $X_ d \subset X$ such that $X = \coprod _{d \geq 0} X_ d$ and $f|_{X_ d} : X_ d \to S$ has relative dimension $d$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediate from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RL" data-tag="00RL">10.130.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>